        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0654" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12266.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Collector Cobb to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>De la Garza, Commercial Agent of General Villa at Juarez, is authority for the
                    following information:</p>
                <p>Generals Carranza and Villa disagreed about Zacatecas campaign. Carranza ordered
                    Villa send soldiers to Natera. Villa insisted on <pb facs="0655" n="539"
                        xml:id="pg539"/> accompanying them. Carranza ordered him to serve under
                    Natera. Villa resigned to Carranza last Saturday [the 13th]. Carranza accepted
                    resignation by telegraph and ordered Villa back to Chihuahua as Governor. Villa
                    and his generals—who are said to have been Angeles, Aguirre, Behavides,
                    Monclova, Herrera, Urbina, Ortega, the two Rodriguez, Contreras, Peireira,
                    Robles and others—met at Torreon last Sunday [the 14th]. They agreed to
                    principle of a civilian for President and demanded that Villa remain their chief
                    military officer, leaving it to Carranza to determine his course.
                    Constitutionalists are seeking to heal the breach. * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
